  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 201 PM MDT THU AUG 6 2026\nThe gradual cooling will end Tuesday when temperatures are only\n3 to 6 degrees above normal under dry zonal flow aloft. Flow \nwill become southwesterly again Wednesday ahead of the next \napproaching north Pacific trough, and monsoon moisture will\nagain advance northward to the NV/ID border, especially into \nand east of Twin Falls County. Thursday's forecast is less clear\nas the GFS brings the next cool upper trough inland while ECMWF\ncompletely eliminates it. We hope for better model consistency \ntonight or tomorrow. Either way, high temperatures should stay \nbelow 100 degrees even under southwest flow aloft, as the main \nupper ridge continues to slowly weaken and shift south.",
